b is ambiguous only when rules.ordering itself leaves ties undefined AND two or more events contest the same (job, revision) pair AND the reachable orderings disagree on that job's final state. Never invent a tie-break.\r\n\r\nReturn only the required JSON object. No prose, no explanation, no code fences.\r\n\r\nprompt:\r\n{\r\n  \"events\": [\r\n    [\r\n      \"e1\",\r\n      \"A\",\r\n      1,\r\n      \"queued\"\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      \"e25\",\r\n      \"A\",\r\n      2,\r\n      \"ready\"\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      \"e35\",\r\n      \"A\",\r\n      2,\r\n      \"blocked\"\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      \"e4\",\r\n      \"B\",\r\n      1,\r\n      \"ready\"\r\n    ]\r\n  ],\r\n  \"request\": \"Replay the stream; report ambiguity, never invent a tie-break.\",\r\n  \"rules\": {\r\n    \"apply_ge\": true,\r\n    \"dedup_on_pair\": true,\r\n    \"ordering\": \"revision; ties undefined\"\r\n  }\r\n}\r\nReturn only the required JSON object. No prose.",
